ethods for effectively consolidating important information into model parameters over extended operation periods.\",\n    \"author\": \"Haoliang Han\",\n    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26806\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-06-26\",\n    \"topics\": [\"LLM memory\", \"long-running agents\", \"parametric consolidation\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Autoformalization of Agent Instructions into Policy-as-Code\",\n    \"description\": \"Presents an autoformalization pipeline that translates agent prompts, MCP tool descriptions, and natural language policy documents into formalized policy-as-code implementations. Aims to bridge the gap between natural language instructions and executable policy code. Accepted at the Second Workshop on Agents in the Wild: Safety, Security, and Beyond (AIWILD), ICML 2026.\",\n    \"author\": \"Adam Mondl, Matthew Maisel, John H. Brock\",\n    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26649\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-06-26\",\n    \"topics\": [\"autoformalization\", \"policy-as-code\", \"agent instructions\", \"AI safety\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"When Does Combining Language Models Help? A Co-Failure Ceiling on Routing, Voting, and Mixture-of-Agents Across 67 Frontier Models\",\n    \"description\": \"Studies when combining language models is beneficial through routing, voting, and mixture-of-agents approaches. Evaluates across 67 frontier models and identifies a 'co-failure ceiling' - a limit beyond which model combination doesn't improve performance.\",\n    \"author\": \"Josef Chen\",\n    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.27288\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-06-26\",\n    \"topics\": [\"model combination\", \"ensemble methods\", \"LLM routing\", \"frontier models\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"AgentX: Towards Agent-Driven Self-Iteration of Industrial Recommender Systems\",\n    \"description\": \"Presents AgentX, an agent-driven self-iteration framework for industrial recommender systems. Authors listed alphabetically, suggesting a large collaborative team effort. Focuses on using agents to continuously improve and adapt recommendation systems.\",\n    \"author\": \"Changxin Lao, Fei Pan, Guozhuang Ma, Han Li, Huihuang Lin, and 40+ others\",\n    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26859\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-06-26\",\n    \"topics\": [\"recommender systems\", \"AI agents\", \"industrial applications\", \"self-iteration\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Diagnosing Task Insensitivity in Language Agents\",\n    \"description\": \"Addresses the problem of task insensitivity in language agents - when agents fail to properly adapt to different task requirements. Provides diagnostic approaches and analysis for understanding when and why language agents exhibit task-insensitive behavior.\",\n    \"author\": \"Jingyu Liu, Xiaopeng Wu, Kehan Chen, Chuan Yu, Yong Liu\",\n    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26918\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-06-26\",\n    \"topics\": [\"language agents\", \"task sensitivity\", \"agent evaluation\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"The Capability Frontier: Benchmarks Miss 82% of Model Performance\",\n    \"description\": \"Argues that current benchmarks fail to capture 82% of model performance, presenting a 'capability frontier' framework. Suggests that benchmark evaluations significantly underestimate the full capabilities of AI models, leading to incomplete assessments of model performance.\",\n    \"author\": \"Bradley Fowler, Ryan Smith, Daniel Thi Graviet, William Myers, Joshua Greaves, Narmeen Fatimah Oozeer, Antía García, Philip Quirke, Amirali Abdullah, Fazl Barez, Shriyash Kaustubh Upadhyay\",\n    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26836\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-06-26\",\n    \"topics\": [\"benchmarks\", \"model evaluation\", \"capability assessment\", \"AI metrics\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Do Safety Guardrails Need to Reason? LeanGuard: A Fast and Light Approach for Robust Moderation\",\n    \"description\": \"Presents LeanGuard, a fast and lightweight approach for robust moderation that questions whether safety guardrails need complex reasoning. Offers efficient moderation without heavy computational overhead, with project page and open-source code/models available.\",\n    \"author\": \"Dongbin Na\",\n    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26686\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-06-26\",\n    \"topics\": [\"AI safety\", \"content moderation\", \"efficient guardrails\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"SKILL-DISCO: Distilling and Compiling Agent Traces into Reusable Procedural Skills\",\n    \"description\": \"Introduces SKILL-DISCO, a method for distilling and compiling agent traces into reusable procedural skills. Enables agents to capture and reuse procedural knowledge from their execution traces, improving efficiency and capability transfer across tasks.\",\n    \"author\": \"Zhongxin Guo, Danrui Qi, Hanwen Gu, Peng Cheng, Yongqiang Xiong\",\n    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26669\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-06-26\",\n    \"topics\": [\"agent skills\", \"knowledge distillation\", \"procedural learning\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Socratic agents for autonomous scientific discovery in high-dimensional physical systems\",\n    \"description\": \"Presents Socratic agents designed for autonomous scientific discovery in high-dimensional physical systems. Uses question-driven (Socratic) approaches to explore and discover patterns in complex physical systems, with 27 pages and 5 figures detailing the methodology.\",\n    \"author\": \"Xianrui Zeng, Pengfei Liu, Yirui Zang, Yang Shen, Fei Yu, Chunlei Yu, Minghao Liu, Yang Du\",\n    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26722\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-06-26\",\n    \"topics\": [\"scientific discovery\", \"autonomous agents\", \"Socratic methods\", \"physical systems\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"EGG: An Expert-Guided Agent Framework for Kernel Generation\",\n    \"description\": \"Presents EGG, an expert-guided agent framework specifically designed for kernel generation. Combines automated agent capabilities with expert guidance to generate efficient and correct kernels for various computational tasks.\",\n    \"author\": \"Yaochen Han, Ke Fan, Hongxu Jiang, Wanqi Xu, Weiyu Xie, Runhua Zhang, Chenhui Zhu, Yixiang Zhang\",\n    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26758\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-06-26\",\n    \"topics\": [\"kernel generation\", \"expert-guided agents\", \"code generation\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Humans Disengage, Reasoning Models Persist: Separating Difficulty Registration from Deliberation Allocation\",\n    \"description\": \"Explores the difference between how humans and reasoning models allocate effort when facing difficult tasks. Humans tend to disengage from difficult problems, while reasoning models persist in deliberation. Discusses separating difficulty registration from deliberation allocation in AI systems.\",\n    \"author\": \"Han-yu Wang\",\n    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26502\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-06-26\",\n    \"topics\": [\"reasoning models\", \"human-AI comparison\", \"deliberation\", \"difficulty assessment\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"KARLA: Knowledge-base Augmented Retrieval for Language Models\",\n    \"description\": \"Presents KARLA, a knowledge-base augmented retrieval approach for language models. Enhances LLM capabilities by integrating structured knowledge bases with retrieval mechanisms, improving factual accuracy and reducing hallucination.\",\n    \"author\": \"Francois Crespin, Fabian M. Suchanek, Nils Holzenberger\",\n    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26807\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-06-26\",\n    \"topics\": [\"retrieval augmentation\", \"knowledge bases\", \"LLM accuracy\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  }\n]",
